Qualification also found that the captured Bootstrap colorpicker compiler
source string uses `rhbq` where the approved source uses `rgba`. Both strings
have 13,640 bytes; the first difference is offset 8804. Eleven other compiler
source strings match their approved files exactly. This is not normalized,
rewritten or claimed equivalent. GitHub #305 records both hashes and the
unverified cause.

The selected folder-group case compares the style/account directory walks;
it does not compile or render that Bootstrap file. Asset enumeration admission
binds the historical approved source snapshot. It does not resolve the distinct
compiler-capture discrepancy or establish Bootstrap compiler-source parity.

